WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.900
The new Game of Thrones Season 8 teaser shows
the crypts of Winterfell – where thousands

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:11.790
of years of dead Starks are entombed .
Jon Snow carries a torch through the darkness,

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:17.270
which fits the imagery of Azor Ahai – a
hero prophesied to defeat the darkness with

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:23.310
a sword called Lightbringer .
Jon passes the tomb of Lyanna Stark. Jon doesn’t

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:29.000
know it, but Lyanna is his mother. She fell
in love with Rhaegar Targaryen, but she died

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.370
giving birth to Jon. Lyanna’s brother Ned
promised to “protect” Jon, by saying that

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:39.310
Jon is his child .
A feather falls from Lyanna’s statue. It

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:45.690
was put there in Season 1 by King Robert,
who had loved Lyanna. In Season 5, Sansa finds

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:50.350
this feather, and talks about how Rhaegar
supposedly kidnapped and raped Lyanna – which

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:56.399
we now know isn’t true . Maybe this feather
represents the truth of Lyanna and Rhaegar’s

00:00:56.399 --> 00:01:03.139
love – and of Jon’s real heritage.
Sansa sees the tomb of her mother Catelyn.

00:01:03.139 --> 00:01:07.740
In the books, Cat is resurrected as a zombie
called Stoneheart, so it’s funny to see

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:14.130
Cat as a statue made of stone. We hear a line
from Season 3 – when Catelyn said she’d

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:19.640
once made a “promise” to love Jon. But
Catelyn found she couldn’t love Jon – cause

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:25.479
she thought he was Ned’s bastard. Cat felt
that this broken promise caused all the “horror”

00:01:25.479 --> 00:01:31.490
that comes to House Stark . So this is a reminder
of how the Stark family has suffered – and

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:35.759
of the pain caused by the secret of Jon’s
birth.

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:40.909
Jon sees the tomb of Ned Stark. We hear a
line from Season 1 – where Ned says that

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:45.619
Jon may be a bastard, but he’s still Ned’s
“blood” – which is true in that Ned

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:51.229
is Jon’s uncle. Ned promises that next time
he sees Jon, they’ll talk about his mother

00:01:51.229 --> 00:01:57.440
. So these three voiceover lines all refer
to promises made about Jon – Ned’s promise

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:02.760
to protect Jon, Cat’s promise to love Jon,
and Ned’s promise to talk about Jon’s

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:09.320
mum. Of course, tragically, Ned dies, and
Jon Snow still knows nothing. So when will

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:13.730
Jon find out about his parents?
There are hints in the books that Jon will

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:19.390
learn the truth in the crypts. Jon has dreams
of the crypts where the statues say “You

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:23.530
are no Stark” . And there are rumours of
a dragon in the crypts – which might be

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:29.650
a metaphor for Jon finding his Targaryen dragon
identity there . In the show, Jon might just

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:34.989
learn the truth from Sam or Bran. [] But either
way, how will Jon react to learning that he’s

00:02:34.989 --> 00:02:40.630
not Ned’s bastard? That his real name is
Aegon , that he’s heir to the Throne ? Will

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:46.909
he start acting like a Targaryen? Riding dragons,
burning enemies, marrying aunts? Or will Jon

00:02:46.909 --> 00:02:53.120
stay true to his Stark identity? [] Rhaegar
is Jon’s father, but Ned is the man who

00:02:53.120 --> 00:03:00.970
raised him. Jon upholds Ned’s legacy and
values – like Ned says, Jon is a Stark . So

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:07.940
just like Theon can be a Greyjoy and a Stark
. Jon can be a Stark and a Targaryen.

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:14.790
Jon, Sansa and Arya see statues of themselves
– representing their deaths. A cold fogs

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:20.250
rolls in, representing the white walkers and
their army of the dead. The fallen feather

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:27.020
freezes, which might mean the death of life
on Westeros. So like Lyanna and Cat and Ned

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:32.189
before them, will Jon Sansa and Arya die this
season? They’re all stronger than they’ve

00:03:32.189 --> 00:03:39.599
ever been. Jon a heroic king, Sansa a political
player, Arya a Faceless assassin. But “all

00:03:39.599 --> 00:03:43.380
men must die” , and this is the end of Game
of Thrones.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:48.579
By the way, it is weird that Bran isn’t
in this trailer – he’s the only living

00:03:48.579 --> 00:03:53.849
Stark not included. Maybe it’s because Bran
has lost his identity by becoming the three-eyed

00:03:53.849 --> 00:03:59.810
raven – will Bran find himself again, or
become a tree-man like the last raven?

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:05.909
So this trailer is about Stark identity, Jon’s
parentage, and the deathly threat of the white

00:04:05.909 --> 00:04:13.299
walkers. But we can go deeper into the crypts.
They are vast and dark and ancient – there

00:04:13.299 --> 00:04:18.790
are lots of theories on what secrets lie within.
In the books, the crypt statues are often

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:23.570
described as “watching” and “listening”
. Sometimes they “seem to stir” , “as

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:29.760
if the dead were rising” . Fans speculate
that the dead Starks might rise to fight for

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:34.131
Winterfell, like the dead in the Lord of the
Rings. Or maybe they’ll be fight for the

00:04:34.131 --> 00:04:39.640
white walkers. Cause fans speculate that the
Starks are descended from the white walkers

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:44.380
and the Night’s King . Maybe the Night’s
Queen is imprisoned deep in the crypts, and

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:49.510
the white walkers are coming to rescue her.
Or maybe the Great Other, the god of the white

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:54.830
walkers , is down there, and Winterfell was
built to contain him. Rhaegar’s harp could

00:04:54.830 --> 00:05:00.260
be down there, or the Horn of Winter, or Hot
Pie’s secret herbs and spices. There’re

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:05.100
lots of possibilities, but this stuff is more
in the books than the show – so we’ll

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:10.250
cover the crypts in another video.
